1
00:00:00,918 --> 00:00:02,085
PREVIOUSLY ON "FRIENDS"...

2
00:00:02,127 --> 00:00:03,712
I CAN'T BELIEVE
YOU WON'T BE THERE.

3
00:00:03,754 --> 00:00:05,631
WHY NOT TAKE
TWO DAYS OFF?

4
00:00:05,673 --> 00:00:07,048
BECAUSE I CAN'T, ROSS.

5
00:00:07,090 --> 00:00:08,133
THIS IS MY WEDDING.

6
00:00:09,009 --> 00:00:10,135
I CAN'T WAIT TO SEE

7
00:00:10,177 --> 00:00:11,929
WHERE YOU'RE GETTING MARRIED.

8
00:00:11,971 --> 00:00:13,597
IT'S THE MOST BEAUTIFUL PLACE.

9
00:00:13,639 --> 00:00:14,974
IT'S RIGHT OVER...

10
00:00:15,014 --> 00:00:16,934
OH, MY GOD!

11
00:00:16,976 --> 00:00:19,812
POSTPONING IT IS NOT AN OPTION.

12
00:00:19,854 --> 00:00:21,605
THIS WEDDING WON'T HAPPEN.

13
00:00:21,647 --> 00:00:23,607
IF YOU DON'T LOVE THIS

14
00:00:23,649 --> 00:00:26,193
WE'LL DO IT ANY OTHER
PLACE, ANY OTHER TIME.

15
00:00:26,234 --> 00:00:27,569
REALLY, IT'S FINE.

16
00:00:27,611 --> 00:00:29,571
IT'S PERFECT.

17
00:00:29,613 --> 00:00:30,572
I'M GOING TO LONDON.

18
00:00:30,614 --> 00:00:31,281
WHAT?!

19
00:00:31,323 --> 00:00:32,449
IT'S NOT OVER

20
00:00:32,491 --> 00:00:33,742
UNTIL SOMEONE SAYS "I DO."

21
00:00:33,784 --> 00:00:34,702
I DO!

22
00:00:34,743 --> 00:00:36,161
I DO, I DO!

23
00:00:36,203 --> 00:00:37,705
RACHEL, NO!

24
00:00:39,289 --> 00:00:40,833
( phone ringing )

25
00:00:43,042 --> 00:00:44,712
THE WALTHAM RESIDENCE.

26
00:00:44,753 --> 00:00:46,881
HI. IS THIS
EMILY'S PARENTS HOUSE?

27
00:00:46,922 --> 00:00:48,674
This is the housekeeper
speaking.

28
00:00:48,716 --> 00:00:50,300
BY THE WAY, YOUNG LADY

29
00:00:50,342 --> 00:00:52,469
THAT IS NOT HOW ONE
ADDRESSES A PERSON

30
00:00:52,511 --> 00:00:53,679
ON THE TELEPHONE.

31
00:00:53,721 --> 00:00:56,640
First, one identifies oneself

32
00:00:56,682 --> 00:01:01,061
AND THEN ASKS FOR THE PERSON
WITH WHOM ONE WISHES TO SPEAK.

33
00:01:01,102 --> 00:01:03,146
( British accent ):
THIS IS PHOEBE BUFFAY.

34
00:01:03,188 --> 00:01:05,148
I WAS WONDERING, PLEASE

35
00:01:05,190 --> 00:01:08,485
IF IT'S NOT TOO MUCH TROUBLE,
PLEASE

36
00:01:08,527 --> 00:01:11,321
MIGHT I SPEAK WITH
MISS EMILY WALTHAM, PLEASE?

37
00:01:11,363 --> 00:01:14,199
MISS WALTHAM
IS AT THE REHEARSAL DINNER

38
00:01:14,241 --> 00:01:17,578
AND IT IS NOT POLITE
TO MAKE FUN OF PEOPLE.

39
00:01:17,619 --> 00:01:19,079
GOOD-BYE.

40
00:01:19,120 --> 00:01:20,455
I'LL BE NICE, I SWEAR.

41
00:01:20,497 --> 00:01:23,166
JUST GIVE ME THE NUMBER
FOR WHERE THEY ARE.

42
00:01:23,208 --> 00:01:27,504
I'M AFRAID I'M NOT AT LIBERTY
TO DIVULGE THAT INFORMATION.

43
00:01:27,546 --> 00:01:30,382
SOMEBODY IS ON THEIR WAY
TO RUIN THE WEDDING.

44
00:01:30,424 --> 00:01:32,467
I HAVE TO WARN SOMEBODY.

45
00:01:32,509 --> 00:01:35,012
SO IF YOU DON'T
GIVE ME THAT NUMBER

46
00:01:35,054 --> 00:01:37,556
I'LL COME OVER THERE
AND KICK YOUR SNOOTY ASS

47
00:01:37,598 --> 00:01:39,850
ALL THE WAY TO
NEW... GLOUCKENSHIRE.

48
00:01:39,892 --> 00:01:41,435
HELLO?

49
00:01:41,476 --> 00:01:42,644
HELLO?!

50
00:01:42,686 --> 00:01:44,688
OOH, SHE KNEW
I COULD KICK HER ASS.

51
00:01:50,903 --> 00:01:55,866
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

52
00:01:55,908 --> 00:01:58,159
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

53
00:01:58,201 --> 00:02:00,412
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

54
00:02:00,454 --> 00:02:05,417
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

55
00:02:05,459 --> 00:02:07,878
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN YOUR DAY ♪

56
00:02:07,920 --> 00:02:10,965
♪ YOUR WEEK, YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

57
00:02:11,006 --> 00:02:14,551
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

58
00:02:14,593 --> 00:02:16,887
♪ WHEN THE RAIN STARTS TO POUR ♪

59
00:02:16,929 --> 00:02:19,556
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

60
00:02:19,598 --> 00:02:21,725
♪ LIKE I'VE BEEN THERE BEFORE ♪

61
00:02:21,767 --> 00:02:24,478
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

62
00:02:24,519 --> 00:02:28,023
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

63
00:02:35,363 --> 00:02:36,782
HEY. HI...

64
00:02:36,824 --> 00:02:37,908
SWEETHEART.

65
00:02:37,950 --> 00:02:38,909
MOM... DAD...

66
00:02:38,951 --> 00:02:41,870
OH, SORRY
WE'RE LATE.

67
00:02:41,912 --> 00:02:44,205
MY FAULT. I INSISTED
ON RIDING THE TUBE.

68
00:02:44,247 --> 00:02:46,500
JUDY, THE KIDS.

69
00:02:46,541 --> 00:02:49,795
JACK, THAT'S WHAT
THEY CALL THE SUBWAY.

70
00:02:49,837 --> 00:02:52,213
OH. I THOUGHT...

71
00:02:52,255 --> 00:02:55,134
DAD, DAD, WE GOT IT,
WE GOT IT.

72
00:02:55,174 --> 00:02:57,260
OH, HERE COMES MY
DAD AND STEPMOM.

73
00:02:57,302 --> 00:02:58,762
MR. AND MRS.
GELLER...

74
00:02:58,804 --> 00:03:00,055
HI, HOW ARE YOU?

75
00:03:00,097 --> 00:03:02,432
THIS IS STEVEN...
AND ANDREA WALTHAM.

76
00:03:02,474 --> 00:03:04,601
HOW DO YOU DO?
VERY NICE TO MEET YOU.

77
00:03:04,643 --> 00:03:06,020
DARLING, THE GELLERS.

78
00:03:06,061 --> 00:03:07,771
DARLING, IT'S
THE GELLERS.

79
00:03:07,813 --> 00:03:10,189
SHE'S VERY SELF-
INVOLVED, YOU KNOW.

80
00:03:10,231 --> 00:03:12,400
I SHOULD NEVER
HAVE MARRIED HER.

81
00:03:14,153 --> 00:03:15,112
SORRY, WHAT?

82
00:03:15,154 --> 00:03:16,113
IT'S THE GELLERS.

83
00:03:16,155 --> 00:03:17,156
WHERE?

84
00:03:17,196 --> 00:03:18,197
WELL, THAT'S ONE

85
00:03:18,239 --> 00:03:20,075
AND THERE'S
ANOTHER ONE.

86
00:03:20,117 --> 00:03:21,118
LOVELY TO MEET YOU.

87
00:03:21,160 --> 00:03:22,201
TERRIBLY NICE OF YOU

88
00:03:22,243 --> 00:03:23,704
TO PAY FOR HALF
THE WEDDING.

89
00:03:23,745 --> 00:03:25,039
THE HELL WITH TRADITION.

90
00:03:25,080 --> 00:03:26,247
WE'RE HAPPY TO DO IT.

91
00:03:26,289 --> 00:03:28,750
WE KNOW HOW EXPENSIVE
WEDDINGS CAN BE.

92
00:03:28,792 --> 00:03:31,210
BESIDES, THIS
MAY BE THE ONLY WEDDING

93
00:03:31,252 --> 00:03:32,379
WE GET TO THROW.

94
00:03:33,421 --> 00:03:36,341
A JOKE THAT'S FUNNY
IN ALL COUNTRIES.

95
00:03:39,178 --> 00:03:41,262
SIR?

96
00:03:41,304 --> 00:03:43,140
WHAT'S IN IT?

97
00:03:43,182 --> 00:03:45,266
GOAT CHEESE,
WATERCRESS AND PANCETTA.

98
00:03:48,937 --> 00:03:50,438
THAT'S NOT FOOD.

99
00:03:50,480 --> 00:03:51,690
NO, I DON'T, NO...

100
00:03:54,359 --> 00:03:56,111
EVERYTHING'S DIFFERENT HERE.

101
00:03:56,153 --> 00:03:57,278
I WANT TO GO HOME.

102
00:03:57,320 --> 00:03:58,780
I-I... MISS MY FAMILY.

103
00:03:58,822 --> 00:04:00,532
I MISS THE COFFEEHOUSE.

104
00:04:00,574 --> 00:04:03,451
I CAN'T EVEN REMEMBER
WHAT PHOEBE LOOKS LIKE.

105
00:04:03,493 --> 00:04:06,121
JOEY, IT'S BEEN
THREE DAYS.

106
00:04:06,163 --> 00:04:07,664
OKAY, YOU'RE JUST...

107
00:04:07,706 --> 00:04:09,166
JUST A LITTLE HOMESICK.

108
00:04:09,208 --> 00:04:12,127
OKAY, WOULD YOU JUST
TRY TO RELAX AND JUST...

109
00:04:12,169 --> 00:04:13,461
JUST ENJOY YOURSELF.

110
00:04:13,503 --> 00:04:15,130
YOU'RE DIFFERENT HERE, TOO.

111
00:04:16,798 --> 00:04:18,926
YOU'RE MEAN IN ENGLAND.

112
00:04:21,011 --> 00:04:22,012
WHAT THE HELL!

113
00:04:22,054 --> 00:04:23,180
WHAT'S UP, DAD?

114
00:04:23,222 --> 00:04:25,224
THIS BILL FOR MY
HALF OF THE WEDDING.

115
00:04:25,265 --> 00:04:26,307
IT'S INSANE.

116
00:04:26,349 --> 00:04:27,642
HOW CAN IT BE
SO MUCH?

117
00:04:27,684 --> 00:04:29,477
THE RECEPTION'S
AT THEIR HOUSE.

118
00:04:29,519 --> 00:04:32,480
FLOWERS, LIQUOR,
RECARPET FIRST FLOOR.

119
00:04:32,522 --> 00:04:33,982
NEW GUEST BATH.

120
00:04:34,024 --> 00:04:35,234
LANDSCAPING.

121
00:04:35,275 --> 00:04:37,360
I'M PAYING TO REMODEL
THIS GUY'S HOUSE.

122
00:04:37,402 --> 00:04:39,404
I'M GOING TO GIVE
THAT SON OF A BITCH

123
00:04:39,446 --> 00:04:40,488
A PIECE OF MY MIND.

124
00:04:40,530 --> 00:04:41,782
DAD.

125
00:04:41,823 --> 00:04:43,158
COME ON. PLEASE

126
00:04:43,200 --> 00:04:45,994
I DON'T WANT ANYTHING
TO UPSET EMILY TONIGHT.

127
00:04:46,036 --> 00:04:49,164
SHE'S HAD A HARD ENOUGH
COUPLE OF DAYS AS IT IS.

128
00:04:49,206 --> 00:04:51,833
HERE. HERE. LET ME
GO TALK TO HIM, OKAY?

129
00:04:51,875 --> 00:04:53,043
WELL, YOU TELL THEM

130
00:04:53,085 --> 00:04:55,170
NO ONE TAKES ADVANTAGE
OF THE GELLERS.

131
00:04:55,212 --> 00:04:56,463
OOH, JACK.

132
00:04:56,504 --> 00:05:01,218
SOMETIMES I FORGET HOW
POWERFUL YOU CAN BE.

133
00:05:05,555 --> 00:05:07,348
AND I'M GOING TO GO GET DRUNK.

134
00:05:12,104 --> 00:05:13,063
OOH, OOH, OOH!

135
00:05:13,105 --> 00:05:14,022
HI.

136
00:05:14,064 --> 00:05:15,356
HELLO.

137
00:05:15,398 --> 00:05:16,608
HELLO.

138
00:05:16,650 --> 00:05:18,860
UM, WHEN IS YOUR NEXT
FLIGHT TO LONDON?

139
00:05:18,902 --> 00:05:21,655
THERE'S ONE LEAVING
IN 30 MINUTES

140
00:05:21,696 --> 00:05:24,074
AND I DO HAVE ONE SEAT LEFT.

141
00:05:24,116 --> 00:05:25,826
OH, THANK YOU, THANK YOU.

142
00:05:25,867 --> 00:05:30,038
THE LAST-MINUTE FARE
ON THIS TICKET IS $2,700.

143
00:05:30,080 --> 00:05:31,539
OH. I JUST
DON'T THINK

144
00:05:31,581 --> 00:05:34,042
I HAVE ENOUGH LEFT
ON MY CREDIT CARD.

145
00:05:34,084 --> 00:05:36,711
WELL, YOU CAN SPLIT IT
WITH ANOTHER CREDIT CARD.

146
00:05:36,753 --> 00:05:38,839
WELL, OKAY,
HOW ABOUT FIVE?

147
00:05:40,548 --> 00:05:41,842
OH, THANK YOU.

148
00:05:41,883 --> 00:05:44,594
I'M JUST GOING TO NEED
TO SEE YOUR PASSPORT.

149
00:05:46,888 --> 00:05:47,973
OKAY, YOU KNOW WHAT?

150
00:05:48,015 --> 00:05:49,808
I DON'T HAVE IT
BUT I CAN TELL YOU

151
00:05:49,850 --> 00:05:51,810
EXACTLY WHERE IT IS
ON MY NIGHTSTAND

152
00:05:51,852 --> 00:05:53,812
AND... OKAY.

153
00:05:53,854 --> 00:05:55,147
BUT YOU KNOW WHAT?

154
00:05:55,189 --> 00:05:57,524
OKAY, I HAVE MY...
I HAVE MY DRIVER'S LICENSE

155
00:05:57,565 --> 00:06:01,653
AND I HAVE A 20.

156
00:06:04,739 --> 00:06:07,242
LOOK, FACE IT: MY FATHER
IS NOT GOING TO PAY

157
00:06:07,284 --> 00:06:08,743
FOR THE BUILT-IN BARBECUE

158
00:06:08,785 --> 00:06:12,122
AND BELIEVE ME, YOU CAN
KISS YOUR GAZEBO GOOD-BYE.

159
00:06:13,540 --> 00:06:16,835
NOW, I MIGHT BE ABLE
TO GET YOU THE NEW LAWN.

160
00:06:16,877 --> 00:06:19,796
AH, THEN YOU HAVE TO GIVE US
THE LAWN ORNAMENTS.

161
00:06:19,838 --> 00:06:22,257
I GO BACK THERE
WITH LAWN ORNAMENTS

162
00:06:22,299 --> 00:06:24,634
HE'S GOING TO LAUGH IN MY FACE.

163
00:06:24,676 --> 00:06:27,346
WILL YOU SAY
SOMETHING, STEVEN?!

164
00:06:27,386 --> 00:06:28,555
PLEASE.

165
00:06:28,596 --> 00:06:32,433
DON'T TAKE THAT
TONE WITH ME.

166
00:06:32,475 --> 00:06:35,687
ALL-ALL RIGHT, YOU CAN.

167
00:06:39,233 --> 00:06:40,359
HI, PHEEBS.

168
00:06:40,399 --> 00:06:44,363
OH, THANK GOD,
YOU CHANGED YOUR MIND.

169
00:06:44,403 --> 00:06:46,365
YOU PROBABLY WANT TO BE ALONE

170
00:06:46,405 --> 00:06:47,782
AND YOU DON'T WANT
TO TALK ABOUT IT.

171
00:06:47,824 --> 00:06:49,826
I WANT YOU TO KNOW I THINK
YOU'RE DOING THE RIGHT THING.

172
00:06:49,868 --> 00:06:50,994
BYE, PHEEBS!

173
00:06:51,036 --> 00:06:52,453
WAIT, WHERE
ARE YOU GOING?!

174
00:06:52,495 --> 00:06:54,039
WHAT ARE YOU DOING?
NO! WAIT!

175
00:06:54,081 --> 00:06:58,835
GOD! WHY AM I ALWAYS PREGNANT
WHEN SHE DOES THAT?!

176
00:07:01,171 --> 00:07:02,964
I'D LIKE
TO TOAST ROSS AND EMILY.

177
00:07:03,006 --> 00:07:04,216
OF COURSE,
MY BIG TOAST

178
00:07:04,258 --> 00:07:05,967
WILL BE TOMORROW
AT THE WEDDING

179
00:07:06,009 --> 00:07:07,844
SO THIS IS
KIND OF MY LITTLE TOAST

180
00:07:07,886 --> 00:07:09,470
OR MELBA TOAST,
IF YOU WILL.

181
00:07:12,349 --> 00:07:13,392
OKAY.

182
00:07:13,433 --> 00:07:15,143
I'VE KNOWN ROSS
FOR A LONG TIME.

183
00:07:15,185 --> 00:07:17,354
IN FACT, I KNEW HIM
WHEN HE WAS GOING OUT

184
00:07:17,396 --> 00:07:18,813
WITH HIS FIRST GIRLFRIEND

185
00:07:18,855 --> 00:07:20,065
AND I THOUGHT THINGS

186
00:07:20,107 --> 00:07:21,900
WERE GOING
TO WORK OUT FOR THEM--

187
00:07:21,942 --> 00:07:23,526
UNTIL HE OVERINFLATED HER.

188
00:07:27,114 --> 00:07:29,199
OH, DEAR GOD.

189
00:07:29,241 --> 00:07:30,367
WHAT?

190
00:07:30,409 --> 00:07:32,327
( phone ringing )

191
00:07:32,369 --> 00:07:34,913
HELLO, WALTHAM INTERIORS.

192
00:07:34,955 --> 00:07:36,331
OH, HI. MRS. WALTHAM?

193
00:07:36,373 --> 00:07:39,042
I NEED TO SPEAK
WITH EITHER ONE OF THE BEST MEN

194
00:07:39,084 --> 00:07:40,585
OR ROSS'S SISTER, MONICA.

195
00:07:40,627 --> 00:07:42,087
WHO IS THIS?

196
00:07:42,129 --> 00:07:43,422
OH, I'M PHOEBE BUFFAY.

197
00:07:43,462 --> 00:07:45,424
I'M ONE OF ROSS'S BEST FRIENDS.

198
00:07:45,465 --> 00:07:47,342
IF YOU'RE ONE
OF ROSS'S BEST FRIENDS

199
00:07:47,384 --> 00:07:48,676
WHY AREN'T YOU HERE?

200
00:07:48,718 --> 00:07:51,972
I CAN'T FLY.
I'M HAVING MY BROTHER'S BABIES.

201
00:07:55,183 --> 00:07:56,810
OH.

202
00:07:56,851 --> 00:07:59,229
AM I ON THE RADIO?

203
00:07:59,271 --> 00:08:00,439
NO. UM...

204
00:08:00,521 --> 00:08:02,399
COULD I TALK TO ONE OF THEM?

205
00:08:02,441 --> 00:08:04,234
IT'S VERY, VERY IMPORTANT.

206
00:08:04,276 --> 00:08:06,111
NO, I'M BORED WITH YOU NOW.

207
00:08:06,153 --> 00:08:07,528
I'M GOING TO CUT YOU OFF.

208
00:08:07,570 --> 00:08:08,947
OH!

209
00:08:08,989 --> 00:08:10,949
AND I'M SURE
WE'RE ALL VERY EXCITED

210
00:08:10,991 --> 00:08:14,202
THAT ROSS AND EMILY ARE GETTING
MARRIED AT MONTGOMERY HALL.

211
00:08:14,244 --> 00:08:17,247
TO THINK-- MY FRIEND
GETTING MARRIED IN MONTY HALL.

212
00:08:18,081 --> 00:08:19,582
OH, COME ON. MONTY HALL.

213
00:08:19,624 --> 00:08:20,834
LET'S MAKE A DEAL!

214
00:08:20,875 --> 00:08:22,210
COME ON, YOU PEOPLE!

215
00:08:22,252 --> 00:08:23,628
ALL RIGHT, FORGET IT.

216
00:08:23,670 --> 00:08:25,797
CONGRATULATIONS,
ROSS AND EMILY.

217
00:08:28,842 --> 00:08:30,093
OKAY.

218
00:08:30,135 --> 00:08:33,596
HEY, BEST MAN NUMBER TWO,
JOEY TRIBBIANI.

219
00:08:33,638 --> 00:08:35,682
ALL RIGHT, I'M NOT GOOD
WITH THE JOKES

220
00:08:35,723 --> 00:08:36,766
LIKE CHANDLER HERE.

221
00:08:36,808 --> 00:08:38,268
BOY...

222
00:08:38,310 --> 00:08:40,270
BUT, UH...

223
00:08:40,312 --> 00:08:41,438
I JUST WANT TO SAY

224
00:08:41,480 --> 00:08:43,857
CONGRATULATIONS
TO THE HAPPY COUPLE.

225
00:08:43,898 --> 00:08:45,525
I FIRST MET ROSS

226
00:08:45,566 --> 00:08:47,652
IN THIS COFFEEHOUSE BACK HOME...

227
00:08:54,659 --> 00:08:57,620
HOME... YEAH.

228
00:08:57,662 --> 00:08:59,080
NEW YORK CITY.

229
00:08:59,122 --> 00:09:00,999
WHERE EVERYBODY KNOWS MY NAME.

230
00:09:04,669 --> 00:09:05,962
WELL, ANYWAY...

231
00:09:06,004 --> 00:09:08,340
UH... I LOVE YOU GUYS...

232
00:09:08,382 --> 00:09:11,343
BUT NOT AS MUCH
AS I LOVE AMERICA.

233
00:09:13,345 --> 00:09:16,473
COULD WE PLEASE
GO HOME NOW?

234
00:09:16,515 --> 00:09:18,266
ARE YOU GOING HOME?

235
00:09:18,308 --> 00:09:22,521
I WAS HOPING TO GET
TO KNOW YOU BETTER.

236
00:09:22,562 --> 00:09:24,856
I'M NOT GOING
ANYWHERE, SWEETHEART.

237
00:09:28,985 --> 00:09:31,279
I WAS LAUGHING.

238
00:09:31,321 --> 00:09:34,949
OUT LOUD?

239
00:09:34,991 --> 00:09:38,119
WELL, I DIDN'T WANT EVERYONE
TO THINK I WAS STUPID.

240
00:09:38,161 --> 00:09:39,496
SO HOW YOU DOING?

241
00:09:39,538 --> 00:09:41,206
MY MOTHER'S
DRIVING ME CRAZY.

242
00:09:41,248 --> 00:09:43,542
BUT ROSS IS GETTING
MARRIED. I'M HAPPY.

243
00:09:43,583 --> 00:09:47,087
I'M NOT GOING TO LET
ANYTHING SPOIL THAT.

244
00:09:47,128 --> 00:09:51,174
I JUST WANT TO SAY THAT ROSS
IS A WONDERFUL YOUNG MAN.

245
00:09:51,216 --> 00:09:53,009
THANKS. WE LIKE HIM.

246
00:09:54,511 --> 00:09:55,970
MY GOD.

247
00:09:56,012 --> 00:09:58,473
YOU MUST HAVE BEEN A TEENAGER
WHEN YOU HAD HIM.

248
00:10:02,185 --> 00:10:05,188
THERE'S NO WAY IN HELL
I'M PAYING FOR IT.

249
00:10:05,230 --> 00:10:07,774
LOOK, WE'RE DOWN
TO JUST ONE POINT.

250
00:10:07,815 --> 00:10:11,194
COULD WE PLEASE MAYBE JUST
SETTLE IT AFTER THE WEDDING?

251
00:10:11,236 --> 00:10:12,987
ALL RIGHT,
BUT I JUST WANT TO SAY

252
00:10:13,029 --> 00:10:14,864
I'M NOT PAYING
FOR YOUR WINE CELLAR

253
00:10:14,906 --> 00:10:18,201
YOU THIEVING,
WOULD-BE-SPEAKING-GERMAN-IF-IT-
WEREN'T-FOR-US

254
00:10:18,243 --> 00:10:19,411
CHEAP LITTLE MAN.

255
00:10:24,249 --> 00:10:25,750
THE GUY WAS HAMMERED, OKAY?

256
00:10:25,792 --> 00:10:28,295
THERE'S NO WAY YOU LOOK
LIKE ROSS'S MOTHER.

257
00:10:28,336 --> 00:10:30,713
THEN WHY WOULD HE SAY IT?

258
00:10:30,755 --> 00:10:32,173
BECAUSE HE'S CRAZY, OKAY?

259
00:10:32,215 --> 00:10:34,384
HE CAME UP TO ME EARLIER
AND THANKED ME

260
00:10:34,426 --> 00:10:36,844
FOR MY VERY MOVING
PERFORMANCE IN TITANIC.

261
00:10:39,055 --> 00:10:40,557
OH, MY MOTHER'S RIGHT.

262
00:10:40,599 --> 00:10:42,683
I'M NEVER GOING
TO GET MARRIED.

263
00:10:42,725 --> 00:10:45,270
YOU KNOW WHAT? THAT IS...

264
00:10:45,312 --> 00:10:47,606
WHO WOULDN'T WANT YOU?

265
00:10:47,688 --> 00:10:48,898
OH, PLEASE.

266
00:10:48,940 --> 00:10:51,109
I'M A SINGLE MOM
WITH A 30-YEAR-OLD SON.

267
00:10:55,780 --> 00:10:58,074
I'M GETTING MARRIED TODAY!

268
00:10:58,116 --> 00:10:59,326
WHOO-HOO!

269
00:10:59,367 --> 00:11:01,077
MORNING, ROSS.

270
00:11:01,119 --> 00:11:02,996
I'M GETTING
MARRIED-- TODAY!

271
00:11:03,037 --> 00:11:04,080
YEAH, YOU ARE!

272
00:11:04,122 --> 00:11:05,332
WHOO-HOO!

273
00:11:06,791 --> 00:11:10,086
DO YOU THINK
HE KNEW I WAS HERE?

274
00:11:16,801 --> 00:11:20,847
WELL, I'VE-I'VE NEVER DONE
THAT WITH YOU BEFORE.

275
00:11:20,888 --> 00:11:22,557
( chuckling ):
NOPE.

276
00:11:22,599 --> 00:11:24,518
SO, UH, HOW ARE YA?

277
00:11:24,559 --> 00:11:26,603
HOW YA... HOW YA...
YOU OKAY?

278
00:11:26,645 --> 00:11:27,604
YEP, YEP.

279
00:11:27,646 --> 00:11:28,647
YOU?

280
00:11:28,687 --> 00:11:30,273
OH, YES, YES.

281
00:11:30,315 --> 00:11:31,316
UH-HUH.

282
00:11:31,358 --> 00:11:32,526
YOU?

283
00:11:34,027 --> 00:11:35,736
WE DID YOU.

284
00:11:38,072 --> 00:11:39,407
WELL...

285
00:11:39,449 --> 00:11:40,741
I BETTER GET GOING.

286
00:11:40,783 --> 00:11:42,160
OH, YEAH, YEAH.

287
00:11:42,202 --> 00:11:43,828
ABSOLUTELY, YEAH.

288
00:11:46,080 --> 00:11:48,041
COULD YOU NOT LOOK?

289
00:11:48,082 --> 00:11:50,001
I DON'T WANT TO LOOK.

290
00:11:56,633 --> 00:11:58,051
( sighing )

291
00:11:58,092 --> 00:12:00,220
( rhythmic tapping )

292
00:12:07,101 --> 00:12:08,687
UH... UH, EXCUSE ME.

293
00:12:08,727 --> 00:12:10,313
YEAH?

294
00:12:10,355 --> 00:12:11,981
IF YOU'RE PLANNING
ON DOING THAT

295
00:12:12,023 --> 00:12:13,483
THROUGHOUT
THE ENTIRE FLIGHT

296
00:12:13,525 --> 00:12:14,317
PLEASE TELL ME NOW,
SO THAT I CAN

297
00:12:14,359 --> 00:12:16,319
TAKE A SEDATIVE.

298
00:12:16,361 --> 00:12:18,154
OR MAYBE SLIP YOU ONE.

299
00:12:18,196 --> 00:12:20,073
SORRY.

300
00:12:20,114 --> 00:12:22,617
IT'S JUST THAT I'M, UH...
I'M KIND OF EXCITED.

301
00:12:22,659 --> 00:12:24,536
I'M, UH, I'M GOING TO LONDON

302
00:12:24,578 --> 00:12:26,954
TO, UH, TO TELL THIS GUY
THAT I LOVE HIM.

303
00:12:32,502 --> 00:12:34,671
( phone rings )

304
00:12:39,092 --> 00:12:40,510
HELLO?

305
00:12:40,552 --> 00:12:42,554
HEY! WHERE THE HELL
HAVE YOU BEEN?

306
00:12:42,596 --> 00:12:44,347
HEY! I SPENT THE NIGHT OUT.

307
00:12:44,389 --> 00:12:46,099
I MET THIS CUTE BRIDESMAID.

308
00:12:46,140 --> 00:12:47,225
SHE IS SO...

309
00:12:47,267 --> 00:12:48,518
I don't want

310
00:12:48,560 --> 00:12:50,061
TO HEAR ABOUT HER.

311
00:12:50,103 --> 00:12:53,607
AH, PHEEBS, YOU KNOW YOU'RE
STILL MY NUMBER-ONE GIRL.

312
00:12:53,648 --> 00:12:56,735
NO! NO, WE HAVE
AN EMERGENCY, OKAY?

313
00:12:56,775 --> 00:12:58,361
RACHEL'S COMING TO LONDON.

314
00:12:58,403 --> 00:13:00,321
OH, GREAT!

315
00:13:00,363 --> 00:13:01,780
NO, IT'S NOT GREAT, NO!

316
00:13:01,822 --> 00:13:04,701
SHE'S COMING TO TELL ROSS
THAT SHE LOVES HIM!

317
00:13:04,743 --> 00:13:05,993
BUT... HE LOVES EMILY.

318
00:13:06,035 --> 00:13:07,537
I KNOW THAT!

319
00:13:07,579 --> 00:13:09,872
YOU HAVE TO STOP HER!

320
00:13:09,914 --> 00:13:11,082
She'll ruin the wedding!

321
00:13:11,124 --> 00:13:12,709
OKAY.

322
00:13:12,751 --> 00:13:14,835
SO I'VE DONE MY PART, OKAY?

323
00:13:14,877 --> 00:13:16,755
IT'S YOUR RESPONSIBILITY NOW.

324
00:13:16,795 --> 00:13:19,173
THE BURDEN IS OFF ME, RIGHT?

325
00:13:19,215 --> 00:13:20,091
RIGHT.

326
00:13:20,133 --> 00:13:22,093
SO TELL ME ABOUT THIS GIRL.

327
00:13:26,931 --> 00:13:28,308
HEY, HAVE YOU
SEEN MONICA?

328
00:13:28,349 --> 00:13:30,101
I'M NOT SEEING MONICA.

329
00:13:33,480 --> 00:13:34,564
WHAT?

330
00:13:34,606 --> 00:13:35,982
WHAT?

331
00:13:36,023 --> 00:13:37,776
WE GOT TO FIND HER.
PHOEBE JUST CALLED.

332
00:13:37,816 --> 00:13:40,027
RACHEL'S COMING TO TELL ROSS
SHE LOVES HIM!

333
00:13:40,069 --> 00:13:41,404
OH, MY GOD!
WE GOT TO

334
00:13:41,446 --> 00:13:43,114
FIND MONICA-- KNOW WHERE SHE IS?

335
00:13:43,156 --> 00:13:45,617
NO, OKAY?!
WHAT'S WITH THE THIRD DEGREE?!

336
00:13:45,659 --> 00:13:48,369
WHY DON'T YOU JUST SHINE
A LIGHT IN MY EYES?!

337
00:13:49,870 --> 00:13:51,289
...AND SO THEN I REALIZED

338
00:13:51,331 --> 00:13:53,416
ALL THIS STUFF
THAT I HAD BEEN DOING:

339
00:13:53,458 --> 00:13:54,959
PROPOSING TO JOSHUA

340
00:13:55,001 --> 00:13:57,796
LYING TO ROSS ABOUT WHY
I COULDN'T COME TO THE WEDDING

341
00:13:57,836 --> 00:13:59,756
WAS ALL JUST A WAY OF...

342
00:13:59,798 --> 00:14:00,757
OH! OH! OH!

343
00:14:00,799 --> 00:14:01,800
I'M SORRY.

344
00:14:01,840 --> 00:14:03,050
CAN I INTERRUPT?

345
00:14:03,092 --> 00:14:05,553
YEAH, I JUST WANT
TO SAY THAT YOU...

346
00:14:05,595 --> 00:14:10,183
ARE A HORRIBLE,
HORRIBLE PERSON.

347
00:14:10,224 --> 00:14:11,184
EH, P-P-PARDON ME?

348
00:14:11,225 --> 00:14:12,644
YOU SAY YOU LOVE
THIS MAN

349
00:14:12,686 --> 00:14:14,521
YET YOU'RE ABOUT TO RUIN
THE HAPPIEST DAY OF HIS LIFE.

350
00:14:14,562 --> 00:14:17,649
I'M AFRAID I HAVE TO AGREE
WITH YOUR FRIEND PHEEBS.

351
00:14:17,691 --> 00:14:21,152
THIS IS A... THIS IS A
TERRIBLE, TERRIBLE PLAN.

352
00:14:21,194 --> 00:14:23,613
BUT HE HAS TO KNOW
HOW I FEEL!

353
00:14:23,655 --> 00:14:24,823
BUT WHY?

354
00:14:24,863 --> 00:14:26,700
HE LOVES THIS...
THIS EMILY PERSON.

355
00:14:26,741 --> 00:14:28,034
NO GOOD CAN COME OF THIS.

356
00:14:28,075 --> 00:14:29,494
( gasping softly )

357
00:14:29,536 --> 00:14:30,995
I THINK
YOU'RE WRONG.

358
00:14:31,037 --> 00:14:32,079
OH, NO!

359
00:14:34,708 --> 00:14:36,501
OH, BY THE WAY,
IT SEEMS

360
00:14:36,543 --> 00:14:39,212
TO BE PERFECTLY CLEAR
THAT YOU WERE ON A BREAK.

361
00:14:39,253 --> 00:14:41,881
( gasping )

362
00:14:49,389 --> 00:14:51,808
OH, MY GOD!

363
00:14:51,850 --> 00:14:53,810
IT'S LIKE A FAIRYLAND.

364
00:14:53,852 --> 00:14:55,144
I KNOW.

365
00:14:55,186 --> 00:14:57,021
IT'S HORRIBLE, ISN'T IT?

366
00:14:57,063 --> 00:14:58,481
WELL, I LOVE IT.

367
00:14:58,523 --> 00:15:00,608
I ONLY HOPE MY WEDDING
LOOKS THIS GOOD.

368
00:15:00,650 --> 00:15:01,735
I JUST HOPE...

369
00:15:01,776 --> 00:15:03,778
YOU CAN LET SOME OF THEM
GO BY.

370
00:15:04,612 --> 00:15:06,072
( whispering ):
PSST! MONICA!

371
00:15:06,113 --> 00:15:08,575
WE REALLY NEED TO START
LOOKING OUT FOR RACHEL.

372
00:15:08,616 --> 00:15:10,243
I'LL COVER THE FRONT DOOR.

373
00:15:10,284 --> 00:15:13,663
YOU WATCH THAT BIG HOLE
AT THE BACK OF THE BUILDING

374
00:15:13,705 --> 00:15:16,165
AND I GOT CHANDLER
COVERING ROSS.

375
00:15:16,207 --> 00:15:18,918
WHY WOULD I CARE
WHERE CHANDLER IS?

376
00:15:18,959 --> 00:15:20,545
YOU KNOW, UH...

377
00:15:20,587 --> 00:15:23,256
SOMETIMES I DON'T
EVEN LIKE CHANDLER.

378
00:15:24,382 --> 00:15:25,759
OKAY.

379
00:15:28,219 --> 00:15:29,345
Ross:
I DO.

380
00:15:29,387 --> 00:15:31,347
I DO.

381
00:15:31,389 --> 00:15:32,724
I DO.

382
00:15:32,766 --> 00:15:35,101
OH, YEAH, YOU'RE RIGHT;
IT'S THE SECOND ONE.

383
00:15:35,142 --> 00:15:36,935
REALLY?

384
00:15:40,064 --> 00:15:41,649
HELLO, JOEY.

385
00:15:41,691 --> 00:15:43,276
HEY, FELICITY.

386
00:15:44,277 --> 00:15:46,696
UM, I THOUGHT
ABOUT YOU ALL DAY.

387
00:15:46,738 --> 00:15:48,072
YEAH?

388
00:15:48,114 --> 00:15:50,575
( giggling ):
TALK NEW YORK TO ME AGAIN.

389
00:15:50,617 --> 00:15:52,869
FUGGETABOUTIT...

390
00:15:52,911 --> 00:15:54,203
MMM....

391
00:15:54,245 --> 00:15:55,830
( deep voice):
HOW YOU DOIN'?

392
00:15:55,872 --> 00:15:56,955
MMM!

393
00:15:56,997 --> 00:15:58,958
OH, YEAH...

394
00:15:59,959 --> 00:16:01,461
THERE'S NOTHING TO DISCUSS.

395
00:16:01,502 --> 00:16:03,254
WE'RE NOT PAYING
FOR YOUR WINE CELLAR.

396
00:16:03,296 --> 00:16:05,506
YOU HAVE TO MEET ME
IN THE MIDDLE HERE.

397
00:16:05,548 --> 00:16:06,883
YOU KEEP PUSHING

398
00:16:06,925 --> 00:16:08,593
MY FOOT WILL MEET
YOUR ASS!

399
00:16:08,635 --> 00:16:10,261
Ross:
DAD!

400
00:16:10,303 --> 00:16:11,262
WHAT'S GOING ON?!

401
00:16:11,304 --> 00:16:12,263
NOTHING, NOTHING.

402
00:16:12,305 --> 00:16:13,640
EVERYTHING'S UNDER CONTROL.

403
00:16:13,681 --> 00:16:14,641
YOU WANT A PIECE OF ME, SIR?

404
00:16:14,682 --> 00:16:15,349
IS THAT WHAT YOU'RE SAYING?

405
00:16:15,391 --> 00:16:18,603
YOU WANT A PIECE OF ME?

406
00:16:18,645 --> 00:16:19,604
Ross:
THAT'S IT!

407
00:16:19,646 --> 00:16:21,522
PARENTS! PARENTS! BACK AWAY!

408
00:16:21,564 --> 00:16:24,024
ALL RIGHT, THIS IS OUR
WEDDING DAY!

409
00:16:24,066 --> 00:16:25,777
FROM NOW ON,
EVERYONE GETS ALONG

410
00:16:25,819 --> 00:16:28,988
AND IF I HEAR ONE MORE WORD

411
00:16:29,029 --> 00:16:30,406
NO GRANDCHILDREN.

412
00:16:30,448 --> 00:16:31,532
THAT'S RIGHT!

413
00:16:31,574 --> 00:16:32,533
OKAY, OKAY.

414
00:16:32,575 --> 00:16:34,243
SORRY, OLD BOY,
SORRY.

415
00:16:34,285 --> 00:16:36,036
SORRY, SORRY.

416
00:16:36,078 --> 00:16:39,791
( muttering ):
I COULD KILL YOU
WITH MY THUMB, YOU KNOW.

417
00:16:43,753 --> 00:16:45,379
WHAT WAS
ALL THAT ABOUT?

418
00:16:45,421 --> 00:16:48,466
( sighing ):
IT WAS THIS
DISAGREEMENT OVER...

419
00:16:48,508 --> 00:16:50,176
( sighing )

420
00:16:50,217 --> 00:16:52,428
MY GOD, YOU...
YOU LOOK BEAUTIFUL.

421
00:16:52,470 --> 00:16:53,805
OH...

422
00:16:53,847 --> 00:16:56,975
YOU ARE NOT MEANT TO
SEE ME BEFORE THE WEDDING.

423
00:16:57,016 --> 00:16:58,100
IT'S BAD LUCK.

424
00:16:58,142 --> 00:16:59,560
YOU KNOW WHAT?

425
00:16:59,602 --> 00:17:00,812
I THINK WE'VE HAD

426
00:17:00,854 --> 00:17:03,481
ALL THE BAD LUCK
WE'RE GOING TO HAVE.

427
00:17:03,523 --> 00:17:05,483
OOH...

428
00:17:37,891 --> 00:17:40,393
MY GOD! RACHEL!

429
00:17:40,434 --> 00:17:42,144
( laughing )

430
00:17:42,186 --> 00:17:43,897
YOU'RE HERE.

431
00:17:43,938 --> 00:17:46,983
I CAN'T BELIEVE IT!

432
00:17:47,025 --> 00:17:48,067
WHAT HAPPENED?

433
00:17:48,108 --> 00:17:49,443
WHY ARE YOU HERE?

434
00:17:49,485 --> 00:17:51,404
WELL, I JUST CAME...

435
00:17:54,866 --> 00:17:57,702
I JUST NEEDED
TO TELL YOU...

436
00:18:00,204 --> 00:18:03,290
CONGRATULATIONS.

437
00:18:10,089 --> 00:18:14,510
( acoustic folk music playing)

438
00:18:29,692 --> 00:18:31,402
( phone ringing )

439
00:18:34,572 --> 00:18:36,198
WALTHAM INTERIORS.

440
00:18:36,240 --> 00:18:37,491
Mrs. Waltham, hi.

441
00:18:37,533 --> 00:18:38,743
It's Phoebe again.

442
00:18:38,785 --> 00:18:41,328
CAN I PLEASE
TALK TO ONE OF THE BEST MEN?

443
00:18:41,370 --> 00:18:43,414
THIS IS THE LAST TIME,
I PROMISE.

444
00:18:43,456 --> 00:18:47,085
JOEY, THERE'S A GIRL
ON THE PHONE FOR YOU.

445
00:18:47,126 --> 00:18:49,963
GREAT!

446
00:18:50,004 --> 00:18:51,422
HELLO.

447
00:18:51,464 --> 00:18:52,673
Joey, it's Phoebe.

448
00:18:52,715 --> 00:18:53,674
DID YOU STOP RACHEL?

449
00:18:53,716 --> 00:18:54,801
It's okay.

450
00:18:54,842 --> 00:18:56,928
SHE JUST CAME AND
GAVE HIM A HUG.

451
00:18:56,970 --> 00:18:58,262
SO, NOTHING GOT RUINED?

452
00:18:58,304 --> 00:18:59,346
No.

453
00:18:59,388 --> 00:19:01,891
OH, THAT'S SO GREAT!

454
00:19:01,933 --> 00:19:03,977
SO, WHAT'S GOING ON NOW?

455
00:19:04,018 --> 00:19:07,146
UH... I'M WALKING
DOWN THE AISLE.

456
00:19:10,190 --> 00:19:11,985
STILL WALKING.

457
00:19:13,569 --> 00:19:15,655
NOW, I'M AT THE
FRONT WITH ROSS.

458
00:19:15,696 --> 00:19:17,197
IT'S PHOEBE.

459
00:19:21,494 --> 00:19:23,621
HE LOOKS PRETTY MAD.

460
00:19:23,663 --> 00:19:25,957
UH... I BETTER GO.

461
00:19:25,999 --> 00:19:27,083
NO, WAIT, WAIT, WAIT!

462
00:19:27,125 --> 00:19:28,626
HOLD IT UP SO I CAN LISTEN!

463
00:19:34,966 --> 00:19:37,343
WHAT WE DID LAST NIGHT WAS...

464
00:19:37,384 --> 00:19:38,886
STUPID.

465
00:19:38,928 --> 00:19:41,764
TOTALLY CRAZY AND STUPID.

466
00:19:41,806 --> 00:19:44,391
WHAT WERE WE THINKING?

467
00:19:44,433 --> 00:19:47,269
BUT I'M COMING
TO YOUR ROOM TONIGHT, RIGHT?

468
00:19:49,271 --> 00:19:50,773
OH, YEAH, DEFINITELY.

469
00:19:50,815 --> 00:19:55,611
( playing
"Here Comes The Bride" )

470
00:20:15,589 --> 00:20:17,050
FRIENDS

471
00:20:17,091 --> 00:20:20,720
FAMILY, WE'RE GATHERED
TO CELEBRATE HERE TODAY

472
00:20:20,761 --> 00:20:23,973
THE JOYOUS UNION
OF ROSS AND EMILY.

473
00:20:24,015 --> 00:20:25,391
MAY THE HAPPINESS

474
00:20:25,432 --> 00:20:27,143
we share with them today

475
00:20:27,185 --> 00:20:28,602
BE WITH THEM ALWAYS.

476
00:20:28,644 --> 00:20:31,022
NOW, EMILY,
REPEAT AFTER ME.

477
00:20:31,064 --> 00:20:32,314
I, EMILY...

478
00:20:32,356 --> 00:20:33,691
I, EMILY...

479
00:20:33,733 --> 00:20:34,859
TAKE THEE,
ROSS...

480
00:20:34,901 --> 00:20:36,152
TAKE THEE, ROSS...

481
00:20:36,194 --> 00:20:37,904
AS MY LAWFULLY
WEDDED HUSBAND

482
00:20:37,945 --> 00:20:39,321
IN SICKNESS
AND IN HEALTH

483
00:20:39,363 --> 00:20:41,615
TILL DEATH PARTS US.

484
00:20:41,657 --> 00:20:44,160
AS MY LAWFULLY WEDDED HUSBAND

485
00:20:44,202 --> 00:20:47,997
IN SICKNESS AND IN HEALTH
UNTIL DEATH PARTS US.

486
00:20:48,039 --> 00:20:49,707
NOW, ROSS

487
00:20:49,749 --> 00:20:52,752
REPEAT AFTER ME.

488
00:20:52,793 --> 00:20:54,712
I, ROSS...

489
00:20:54,754 --> 00:20:56,296
I, ROSS...

490
00:20:56,338 --> 00:20:57,840
TAKE THEE, EMILY...

491
00:20:57,882 --> 00:20:59,592
TAKE THEE, RACHEL...

492
00:21:03,470 --> 00:21:04,513
EMILY.

493
00:21:09,435 --> 00:21:10,770
( chuckles nervously )

494
00:21:10,811 --> 00:21:11,938
EMILY.

495
00:21:17,110 --> 00:21:19,528
UH...

496
00:21:19,570 --> 00:21:22,240
SHALL I GO ON?

497
00:21:43,469 --> 00:21:46,847
Captioned by
The Caption Center
WGBH Educational Foundation]

